            "review_title": "Review at Moku Japanese Restaurant",
            "review_text": "Dr. Clemen Chiang\nSingapore, Singapore59 contributions\n1\nHeavenly Experience of Wine & Dine in Saigon\nMar 2019 • Friends\nI've visited Saigon several times before I discovered this hidden gem! \n\nUpon arrival, our group was well greeted by an entourage of happy waiters and waitresses. The smartly dressed Chef welcomed us and gave a bow.\n\nAt the garden, there was a Japanese koi pond swimming right under us! So many fishes swimming along man-made \"mountains\" with a sight that is beholding.\n\nOur food was served with a sort of exquisiteness that is befitting of a Michelin treatment. Good food; glorious food. Then of course, the Japanese sake!\n\nThis magical place is excellent for hosting customers as well as families. During our visit, there was a couple with two kids who were well take care of by the restaurant staff. This makes everyone happy.\n\nExcellent! I recommend this restaurant highly and a must visit destination in Saigon.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nWritten March 29, 2019",
            "rating": 5.0,
